...
	&lt;parameter name=&quot;passwordType&quot; value=&quot;PasswordDigest&quot; /&gt;
...
&lt;/deployment&gt;
</pre>

At a minimum, only allow trusted users to access the service list and ensure that unnecessary services are not exposed. However, it is recommended that you disable the ability to list services all together.

The following configuration shows how to prevent services from being listed:
<pre>
&lt;deployment xmlns=&quot;http://xml.apache.org/axis/wsdd/&quot; xmlns:java=&quot;http://xml.apache.org/axis/wsdd/providers/java&quot;&gt;
...
  &lt;parameter name=&quot;axis.disableServiceList&quot; value=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;
...
&lt;/deployment&gt;
</pre>

Description.Explanation:
Any part of a message that is not signed has the potential to be intercepted and modified without being detected by the receiver. Without a signature, a receiver cannot cryptographically verify that the contents of a message are authentic.

The following service provider configuration tells Axis 2 to accept unsigned messages:
<pre>
&lt;service&gt;
...
	&lt;parameter name=&quot;InflowSecurity&quot;&gt;
		&lt;action&gt;
			&lt;items&gt;Timestamp Encrypt&lt;/items&gt;
			...
		&lt;/action&gt;
	&lt;/parameter&gt;
&lt;/service&gt;
</pre>

Description.Recommendations:
Configure the service to verify the signature on incoming requests.

The following service provider configuration tells Axis 2 to verify signatures:
<pre>
&lt;service&gt;
...
	&lt;parameter name=&quot;InflowSecurity&quot;&gt;
		&lt;action&gt;
			&lt;items&gt;Timestamp Signature Encrypt&lt;/items&gt;
			...
		&lt;/action&gt;
	&lt;/parameter&gt;
&lt;/service&gt;
</pre>

Description.Explanation:
Any part of a message that is not signed has the potential to be intercepted and modified without the modification being detected by the receiver. Without a signature, a receiver cannot cryptographically verify the integrity or origin of the message contents.

The following service provider configuration tells Axis 2 to send unsigned timestamps:
<pre>
&lt;service&gt;
...
	&lt;parameter name=&quot;OutflowSecurity&quot;&gt;
		&lt;action&gt;
			&lt;items&gt;Timestamp Encrypt&lt;/items&gt;
			...
		&lt;/action&gt;
	&lt;/parameter&gt;
&lt;/service&gt;
</pre>

Description.Recommendations:
Configure the service to sign outgoing messages.

The following service provider configuration tells Axis 2 to sign outbound messages:
<pre>
&lt;service&gt;
...
	&lt;parameter name=&quot;OutflowSecurity&quot;&gt;
		&lt;action&gt;
			&lt;items&gt;Timestamp Signature Encrypt&lt;/items&gt;
			...
		&lt;/action&gt;
	&lt;/parameter&gt;
&lt;/service&gt;
</pre>

Order is important! Placing the <code>Signature</code> directive before the <code>Encrypt</code> directive and after the <code>Timestamp</code> directive ensures that the timestamp will be signed and that both the signature and the timestamp will be encrypted.

